-- title:
--   Special-fibre points with stalk dimension ≤ 1 are the η(v)
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_{0}$ and $q$ with $N_{0}$ nonzero and $q$ prime, and assume $q \nmid N_{0}$; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package at level $(N_{0},q)$, that is, a proper, flat, locally finitely presented and integral model of the Igusa-type modular curve over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation $R_{q}$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ at $q$, normal on affine opens, together with a curve model of the modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identified with its generic fibre, the associated Galois equivariance and chart-pinning data, smoothness and geometric integrality of relative dimension $1$ of the generic fibre, and the distinguished sections. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring homomorphism $\rho_{O} \colon R_{q} \to O$ such that the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $q$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa \colon O \to \kappa$. Assume the site hypotheses $H$: the node set of the reduction is finite, the oriented crossing charts and étale-neighbourhood data exist, the assignment of a point $x_{n} \in X_{O}$ to a node $n$ is injective with each $x_{n}$ closed, and the model hypotheses for $q$ and $O$ hold. Assume further that each of the two points $\xi j$ lies in the open set $X_{0}$ of the chart input $C$, namely the complement of the (finite) union of the node points $x_{n}$. Then for every point $y$ of the glued scheme $Y$, the colimit of the glue diagram, if the structure morphism $Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ (the map to the Deligne–Rapoport model followed by its projection) does not send $y$ into the basic open of $q$, so that $y$ lies over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} O$, and if the Krull dimension of the stalk of $Y$ at $y$ is at most $1$, then $y = \eta(v)$ for some index $v$, where $\eta$ is the family of distinguished points attached to the chart data.
--
--   This is the codimension statement for the glued resolution of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_{0}(N_{0}q)$ over an unramified discrete valuation ring: the points of the special fibre whose local ring has dimension at most $1$ are exactly the generic points of its components, namely the two strict branches coming from the $\xi j$ and the generic points of the exceptional lines inserted at the nodes. It is one of the fields of the level-$(N_{0},q)$ package produced by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam).
